{"name":"Sooty Lashes","hex":"#474d52","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sooty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or producing soot.","Soiled with soot"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To blacken or make dirty with soot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sooty"},{"term":"lashes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of lash"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of lash"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lashes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sooty","blocks":[{"text":"Sooty is a British children's television media franchise created by Harry Corbett incorporating primarily television and stage shows. The franchise originated with his fictional glove puppet character introduced to television in The Sooty Show in 1955. The main character, Sooty, is a mute yellow bear with black ears and nose, who is kind-hearted but also cheeky. Sooty performs magic tricks and practical jokes, and squirts his handler and other people with his water pistol. The franchise itself also includes several other puppet characters who were created for television, as well as an animated series, two spin-off series for the direct-to-video market, and a selection of toy merchandising."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Sooty_Logo_%281996-present%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sooty"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9b/Sooty2011.png/250px-Sooty2011.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9b/Sooty2011.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9b/Sooty2011.png/250px-Sooty2011.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser